{"title":"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the numbers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/d/4fd03d5b164ae8b40db27a6f8ddb20d9d43f95fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/52144423e89ff8e005879d327ef189abe7ae3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$81\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af37fa0421381388e7baaa2a3c8786a8d327b22b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.801$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> are arranged from smallest to largest, the correct order is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/f/2eff4b506a1e662d08aaefbad9c3ff3683d64090.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ \\frac{4}{5}, 81\\%, 0.801 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 81\\%, 0.801, \\frac{4}{5}  \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 0.801, \\frac{4}{5}, 81\\%  \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 81\\%, \\frac{4}{5}, 0.801 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ \\frac{4}{5}, 0.801, 81\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"807\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/f/c4fc7e6a18067a2435996e2564a1b513597a4b77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{5} = 0.8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"62\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/1/91100830e7bc244851130c42ea6ffeca9d07d414.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$81\\% = \\frac{81}{100} = 0.81$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"147\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Thus, ordering the three numbers from smallest to largest gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/b/2fbe527db7e97c8d6bb312e1cf54967f4d650547.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf{(E)} \\frac{4}{5}, 0.801, 81\\%}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"145\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can also put everything in terms of thousandths, and then compare the numerators:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/b/4eb55a0fb49438c8397185ac22a94ae9d6fbed0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{5} = \\frac{4 * 200}{5 * 200} = \\frac{800}{1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"161\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a7b6ad0bef127da70a08020c3f9c5ca54e221aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$81\\% = \\frac{810}{1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"100\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/6/b96d7fb6ab1751fa6048460b65b105ba76cd48a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.801 = \\frac{801}{1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"108\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Thus, ordering the three numbers from smallest to largest gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/b/2fbe527db7e97c8d6bb312e1cf54967f4d650547.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf{(E)} \\frac{4}{5}, 0.801, 81\\%}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"145\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/in